.TH std::inplace_vector::back 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::inplace_vector::back \- std::inplace_vector::back

.SH Synopsis
constexpr reference back();             \fB(1)\fP (since C++26)
constexpr const_reference back() const; \fB(2)\fP (since C++26)

Returns a reference to the last element in the container.

Calling back on an empty container causes undefined behavior.

.SH Parameters

\fI(none)\fP

.SH Return value

Reference to the last element.

.SH Complexity

Constant.

.SH Notes

For a non-empty container c, the expression c.back() is equivalent to *std::prev(c.end()).

.SH Example


// Run this code

#include <cassert>
#include <inplace_vector>

int main()
{
    std::inplace_vector<char, 4> letters{'a', 'b', 'c', 'd'};
    assert(letters.back() == 'd');
}

